===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|mineral coal, uncountable, in general}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} A [[black]] or [[brownish]] black [[rock]] formed from [[prehistoric]] [[plant]] [[remains]], [[composed]] largely of [[carbon]] and [[burn]]ed as a [[fuel]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''coal''' in this region was prized by ironmasters in centuries past, who mined it in the spots where the drainage methods of the day permitted.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1947|month=January and February|author=O. S. Nock|title="The Aberdonian" in Wartime|journal=Railway Magazine|pages=3, 5|text='''Coal'''-eaters they may have been, but a more willing or harder working Atlantic engine was never designed.}}
## {{senseid|en|mineral coal, uncountable, as a commodity}} {{lb|en|countable}} A [[type]] of coal, such as [[bituminous]], [[anthracite]], or [[lignite]], and [[grade]]s and [[variety|varieties]] thereof, as a fuel commodity ready to buy and burn.
##: <small>See also:</small> {{l|en|stockpile|id=stock of coal or ore in commerce}}
##: {{ux|en|Put some '''coal''' on the fire.}}
##: {{ux|en|Order some '''coal''' from the coalyard.}}
# {{senseid|en|mineral coal, countable piece}} {{lb|en|countable}} A [[piece]] of coal used for [[burn]]ing {{q|this use is less common in American English}}
#: {{ux|en|Put some '''coals''' on the fire.}}
# {{senseid|en|a hot coal or its remnant}} {{lb|en|countable}} A [[glow]]ing or [[charred]] [[piece]] of coal, [[wood]], or other [[solid]] [[fuel]].
#: {{ux|en|Just as the campfire died down to just '''coals''', with no flames to burn the marshmallows, someone dumped a whole load of wood on, so I gave up and went to bed.}}
#: {{cot|en|ember|ash|clinker}}
# {{senseid|en|charcoal}} [[charcoal]].
# {{lb|en|internet slang|4chan slang}} Content of low quality.
#: {{ux|en|I'm so sick of seeing this left-wing '''coal''' online.}}
# {{lb|en|military slang|WWI|_|–|_|WWII}} [[bomb|Bombs]] [[emit]]ting [[black]] smoke on [[impact]].<ref>{{R:en:Lighter:1972|page=34}}</ref>

